Cell["\<\
For example, starting from one generator of C4, repeated multiplication \
produces its four elements. The returned list always begins with the \
identity; the trivial group is therefore {E}, not an empty list.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d5a24dfe-8e03-4bff-8c4d-a7d286c4c848"],

Cell["\<\
The caller supplies both multiplication and equality because \
magnetic-space-group and spin-space-group elements need not use the same \
concrete product.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"79951735-51eb-457f-83f1-62f573cf29b6"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "549720f8-3bea-4b99-ba9b-6e2ed4feaa99"], "SameTest", "SameQ", Cell["\<\
Binary predicate used to decide whether two generated concrete elements are \
equal. It must return True or False for every pair.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"82b192aa-2b22-4274-b4e3-f0b7f9ebea3d"]}
